00:54:03.720 --> 00:54:11.620
There was an alternate history where Super Mario Brothers 2 was not just a harder Super

00:54:11.620 --> 00:54:16.800
Mario Brothers 1, but might've been its own game that felt more like Super Mario Brothers

00:54:16.800 --> 00:54:17.940
1. Let, let me explain.

00:54:18.100 --> 00:54:19.800
This is, this is our development section.

00:54:19.960 --> 00:54:26.360
If you will. There was a sequel prototype, uh, built by Miyamoto and his team, uh, that didn't have,

00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:29.140
I don't think it had the Mario sprites in there or whatever, but it was working on the

00:54:29.140 --> 00:54:35.880
idea of Mario and Luigi playing cooperatively and they have to lift each other up and throw

00:54:35.880 --> 00:54:40.040
each other, uh, stacking objects and stuff and scrolling the screen upward.

00:54:40.560 --> 00:54:43.600
The design became a little too complex for the Famicom hardware.

00:54:43.820 --> 00:54:47.200
You have to remember they eventually phased that out and went to the Famicom disk system.

00:54:47.200 --> 00:54:51.820
So they didn't like how that gameplay system worked out and they moved away from it, but

00:54:51.820 --> 00:54:52.640
there was an opportunity.

00:54:52.640 --> 00:54:58.240
And I think we see a lot of Super Mario Brothers 2's, uh, you know, lifting and stacking stuff

00:54:58.240 --> 00:54:59.160
still in there.

00:54:59.360 --> 00:55:03.560
Uh, so it's kind of neat to think that they were always thinking about making a game with

00:55:03.560 --> 00:55:04.620
that concept in mind.

00:55:04.860 --> 00:55:11.700
Yeah. So did they ever like, I mean, I know that this game is pretty much that and that, uh,

00:55:12.580 --> 00:55:17.200
um, that element made its way into it, but did they ever like fully do that?

00:55:17.320 --> 00:55:21.060
I haven't played many of the, uh, more, more recent Mario games.

00:55:21.220 --> 00:55:24.540
So, you know, it's funny because the closest thing I can think of, I don't know if anybody

00:55:24.540 --> 00:55:31.760
has played it, but in the Mario RPG, uh, franchise, I think this, I think it was either Superstar

00:55:31.760 --> 00:55:38.420
Saga or, uh, Dream Team, one of them uses the idea of like picking up the other character

00:55:38.420 --> 00:55:43.320
and like A button does one thing for Mario and B button does something for Luigi and doing

00:55:43.320 --> 00:55:47.300
stuff like that. But it doesn't have anything to do with a vertical emphasis or anything.

00:55:47.300 --> 00:55:48.620
It just has to do with interaction.

00:55:48.960 --> 00:55:54.180
But I wonder if they just like have a list of unused ideas that when they go to Mario

00:55:54.180 --> 00:55:56.120
games, they just say like, Oh, let's use that.

00:55:56.280 --> 00:56:01.180
Yeah, I'm sure. But of course the game that, that this was eventually they just wound up making it into

00:56:01.180 --> 00:56:02.220
Doki Doki Panic.

00:56:02.380 --> 00:56:06.800
And instead of lifting other players and playing cooperatively, you just pick up vegetables

00:56:06.800 --> 00:56:08.380
and stack enemies and stuff.

00:56:08.480 --> 00:56:10.380
Cause there's definitely times for that.

00:56:10.500 --> 00:56:12.080
So to get my, my history straight here.

00:56:12.200 --> 00:56:17.100
So then they, they started developing this Super Mario Brothers 2, scrapped it and said,

00:56:17.100 --> 00:56:17.900
okay, this isn't working.

00:56:18.140 --> 00:56:22.160
Let's make this, but let's use some of these elements and make Doki Doki Panic.

00:56:22.540 --> 00:56:25.760
And then they made what came out in Japan as Super Mario Brothers 2.

00:56:25.880 --> 00:56:29.580
And then they took Doki Doki Panic and then re-skinned it as Super Mario Brothers 2, which

00:56:29.580 --> 00:56:30.940
is what it was originally going to be.

00:56:31.400 --> 00:56:32.620
Correct. That's crazy.

00:56:32.720 --> 00:56:33.520
I never knew that.

00:56:33.880 --> 00:56:39.360
And I think, you know, one thing to note there is that Super Mario Brothers 2, Doki Doki

00:56:39.360 --> 00:56:42.720
Panic, that was never like a Nintendo of Japan idea.

00:56:42.720 --> 00:56:45.920
They didn't really like give too much stock to this.

00:56:45.920 --> 00:56:50.540
It was really Nintendo of America who pushed for the idea of like, you don't understand.

00:56:50.540 --> 00:56:57.480
We just had a video game crash over here in 1983 because of games looking all too the

00:56:57.480 --> 00:57:01.140
same and, you know, no way to like get good quality.

00:57:01.320 --> 00:57:04.220
Your whole thing is this Nintendo seal of quality.

00:57:04.440 --> 00:57:09.320
